      "problem": "${}_{6}{P}_{1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ and $r=1$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{6}{P}_{1} & =\\frac{6!}{(6-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
